// Cs14.grammar — C# 14.0: extension container (T3.14.1).
//
// The `extension` container is a TYPE-LEVEL declaration that holds extension properties /
// indexers / events / operators / fields. It has NO name (an identifier after `extension` is
// ERR_ExtensionDisallowsName), an OPTIONAL type-parameter list, a REQUIRED parameter list (at
// least one — Roslyn requireOneElement:true), optional `where` constraints, and a body:
//   extension (this int x)
//   {
//       public static string ToHex() { return x.ToString("X"); }
//   }
//   (or: extension (this int x) ; )
//
// Roslyn refs (C:\RSDN\roslyn, main, src/Compilers/CSharp/Portable/Parser/LanguageParser.cs):
//   * ParseMainTypeDeclaration (1789-1928): the common parser for class/struct/interface/record/
//     extension. For `extension`: name = null (1811-1818); typeParameters = ParseTypeParameterList()
//     (1824, optional); paramList = ParseParenthesizedParameterList(forExtensionOrUnion: true)
//     (1827-1828, requireOneElement:true at 4851) — REQUIRED; baseList = null (1830);
//     where-clauses (1839-1843); body `{ members* }` or `;` (1847-1914).
//   * IsExtensionContainerStart (3396-3401): ExtensionKeyword + (feature enabled or `<` follows).
//   * Dispatch: ParseMemberDeclaration -> IsExtensionContainerStart -> ParseMainTypeDeclaration
//     (3261-3263); IsTypeDeclarationStart -> IsExtensionContainerStart (2501-2503);
//     ParseTypeDeclaration -> IdentifierToken(ExtensionKeyword) -> ParseMainTypeDeclaration (1780-1782).
//   * Version gate — the `extension` container is a C# 14.0 feature (MessageID.IDS_FeatureExtensions,
//     MessageID.cs, C# 14 block). The PARSER accepts the form wherever the rule exists; version
//     purity comes from the rule being Cs14-only (absent at v<=13).
//
// T0.3 merge: re-declaring TypeDeclaration APPENDS ExtensionDeclaration to the Cs1 union
// (Cs1.grammar:27-32) — the same pattern as the Cs9 record (Cs9.grammar:59-60). `extension` is NOT
// a reserved keyword, so the only rule that can match a declaration LEADING with `extension` followed
// by `(` is ExtensionDeclaration: the Cs1 ClassDeclaration/StructDeclaration/... alternatives all
// require a declaration keyword (class/struct/...) after optional attributes/modifiers, so they FAIL
// on `extension` (no equal-length tie). At v<=13 the ExtensionDeclaration alternative is ABSENT, so
// `extension ( ... )` matches no TypeDeclaration alternative and REJECTS (version purity).
//
// The parameter list reuses Cs1 Parameter (Cs1.grammar:472); the `this` parameter modifier is the
// Cs3 feature (Cs3.grammar:245-251), present at v14. The body reuses Cs1 ClassBody
// (Cs1.grammar:102). TypeParameterList (Cs2.grammar:51) and ConstraintClause (Cs2.grammar:107) are
// reused for the optional type-parameter list and the optional `where` constraints.
//
// Meta-grammar note: `|` is not allowed inside a group (CsNitraParser.cs:103), so the
// `( ClassBody | ";" )` body is the named union ExtensionBody (same workaround as Cs1 MethodBody).

// === Type declaration union: APPEND ExtensionDeclaration (T0.3 merge, like the Cs9 record). ===
TypeDeclaration =
    | ExtensionDeclaration;

// Extension container (C# 14.0). `extension` + optional type-parameter list + REQUIRED
// parameter list (at least one) + optional `where` constraints + body (block or `;`).
ExtensionDeclaration = "extension" TypeParameterList? ExtensionParameterList ConstraintClause* ExtensionBody;

// The extension parameter list: "(" (Parameter,)+ ")" — comma-separated, at least one (Roslyn
// requireOneElement:true). Mirrors Cs1 ParameterList (Cs1.grammar:465) = (Parameter; ",")+ wrapped in
// parens. Reuses Cs1 Parameter (Cs1.grammar:472) (the `this` modifier is the Cs3 feature, Cs3.grammar:251).
ExtensionParameterList = "(" (Parameter; ",")+ ")";

// The extension body: a block (`{ members* }`, reusing Cs1 ClassBody) or `;`. Named union (the
// meta-grammar forbids `|` inside a group, CsNitraParser.cs:103) — same workaround as Cs1 MethodBody.
ExtensionBody =
    | ClassBody
    | ";";

// === ref field (T3.14.2, C# 14.0). ===
// A `ref` field is a field declared with the `ref` modifier: `ref int _value;` (and `ref readonly
// int _value;`). Roslyn parses it through the STANDARD field-declaration path (ParseNormalFieldDeclaration,
// LanguageParser.cs:5200-5220): `ref` is a general declaration modifier (GetModifierExcludingScoped,
// LanguageParser.cs:1322-1323 -> DeclarationModifiers.Ref), consumed by the any-order ParseModifiers loop
// (1347) and riding in the field's modifiers list. The binder folds `ref`/`ref readonly` into the type
// (SkipRefInField, SourceMemberFieldSymbol.cs:533-534; RefKind.Ref / RefKind.RefReadOnly) and enforces the
// C# version (IDS_FeatureRefFields, MessageID.cs:262/557 — a "semantic check"), so the PARSER accepts the
// form and the version gate is the binder's concern.
//
// The grammar models `ref` as a MODIFIER (consistent with Cs7 MethodModifier `ref` return, Cs7.grammar:237,
// and Cs7 StructModifier `ref struct`, Cs7.grammar:512): re-declare FieldModifier (append, T0.3 merge) to
// add "ref" to the Cs1 union (Cs1.grammar:155-165) + Cs11 `required` (Cs11.grammar:93). The Cs1 Field
// (Cs1.grammar:148) then consumes `ref` as a field modifier and parses Type + VariableDeclarator.
//
// Disambiguation (longest-match, no equal-length tie):
//   * `ref int x;` (a ref FIELD): Field -> FieldModifier=ref, Type=int, VariableDeclarator=x, ; (matches).
//     Method (Cs7 MethodModifier=ref) -> MethodModifier=ref, Type=int, TypeName=x, then `(` expected but
//     `;` found -> FAILS. So Field is the sole match.
//   * `ref int M() { }` (a ref RETURN method, Cs7): Field -> FieldModifier=ref, Type=int,
//     VariableDeclarator=M, then `;`/`,` expected but `(` found -> FAILS; Method -> MethodModifier=ref,
//     Type=int, TypeName=M, (), MethodBody (matches). So Method is the sole match (no regression).
//
// Version purity: at v<=13 `ref` is NOT a FieldModifier, so `ref int x;` -> FieldModifier* matches zero,
// Type=ref fails (ref is a reserved keyword, Cs1.grammar:632) -> Field FAILS; Method FAILS (no `(` after
// the name) -> no member alternative matches -> REJECTS. At v14 the merged FieldModifier consumes `ref`.
FieldModifier =
    | "ref";
